at long last the first full trailer for  venom has arrived the film which focuses  on Tom Hardy as journalist Eddie Brock  is the second big screen appearance of  every comic fans favorite alien symbiote  after the first teaser of the film  conveyed more about the tone of venom  than its actual content fans finally  have their first real look at what this  movie will be about and more importantly  what Venom's iconic costume is going to  look like this time around the venom  trailer shows us glimpses of Hardy's  Brock the villainous life foundation and  plenty more  amid the explosions alien symbiote  attacks and sinister narration there are  a number of key plot points and details  the trailer offers that you might have  missed the first time around here are  some of the small details you may have  missed in the venom trailer a lethal  protector there are a ton of great  comics that depict venom as a hero  the most notable recent ones don't even  feature Eddie Brock in the starring role  as such there are only so many venom  comics from which the film could draw  inspiration and from the trailer it  looks like the film will be a loose  adaptation of venom lethal protector the  90s miniseries sees venom and Eddie  relocating to San Francisco as fugitives  from spider-man and the authorities they  do so under an agreement that as long as  they don't hurt anyone and stay out of  Spidey's business spider-man will stay  out of theirs the book features them  taking on Carlton Drake in The Life  Foundation both of which appear in the  trailer voice of the people  fans that the character may find  themselves pleasantly surprised by the  direction in which venom takes Eddie  Brock when it comes to his career choice  the prior big screen incarnation of the  character from spider-man 3 depicts  Eddie Brock as a photographer and a  pretty skeevy one at that from the looks  of it venom will set Brock on a  different path one with ties to some of  the characters best comic appearances  the Eddie Brock will get in the film  looks to be an investigative journalist  a career the character had in the  original spider-man comics where he  first appeared the venom lethal  protector comic series further  establishes Brock as having been  inspired by journalists to coverage of  the Watergate scandal which gave Brock  an underlying anti-authoritarian streak  if you translate the film very well it's  a smart decision  for a version of venom that looks to be  more antihero than supervillain as an  investigative journalist Brock should  have a strong sense of right and wrong  and we get a look at his willingness to  make bad people uncomfortable in the  name of truth in the venom trailer it's  a great character decision and bodes  well for Brock as a likable protagonist  a dapper villain the venom trailer also  gives us our first real look at the  film's villain  Carlton Drake played by RZA men Drake is  another carryover from lethal protector  albeit one with which the filmmakers  seemed to have taken a few liberties in  the comics Drake is an older man running  the life foundation he's a shady dude  but he's not responsible for Veneman  Eddie's bonding nor for the discovery of  the original symbiotes although he does  discover the existence of others it  looks like a meds take on the character  will be significantly different Hamed is  young and attractive and by the looks of  it he'll be a prominent media figure in  the world of the film  he's also far more directly tied to the  symbiotes presence on earth with his  life foundation seeming to be  responsible for either discovering the  symbiotes or bringing them to earth to  begin with it makes for a villain far  more directly tied to the protagonist  and that's likely going to be a good  thing love is in the air we get our  first look at the dynamic between Tom  Hardy's Eddie Brock and Michelle  Williams and weighing in the venom  trailer as well and the comics weighing  is Brock's ex-wife even though they  appear to be together in the cinematic  take their relationship may still be a  bit complicated since in the comics she  also eventually gets a symbiote of her  own and becomes the villainous schieben  with multiple symbiotes at play in the  film let's not rule out an appearance  from that particular alter ego just yet  a complicated relationship the  relationship between a host and the  symbiote in Marvel Comics isn't  necessarily defined by a strict set of  rules but generally speaking there is  usually a decision made on the part of  the host to bond with  why would we do that here it's not clear  how much of a choice Eddie Brock has  about sharing his body Eddie doesn't  even seem to understand what's happening  to him during the bonding process and  when his venom powers are finally  unleashed on the men who come to his  apartment looking for their boss's  property he seems just as shocked by  what happens as they are it's a pretty  cool storytelling choice one that opens  up possible explorations of body horror  and Eddie's loss of autonomy as the  hosts cemented by the symbiotes chilling  line so venom will not only have a mind  of his own in the film but also a voice  we hear him speaking to Eddie in the  trailer  since there are obviously two distinct  and separate characters that happen to  occupy the same body we're all in for  the inevitable struggle for control of  dominance between the two one giant leap  for mankind  the Venom symbiote origins story of the  comics is a little bit complicated but  basically spider-man finds the Venom  symbiote while he's in another dimension  fighting in the beyonders secret wars  with the rest of the Marvel Universe and  since Peter Parker's being shared  between Marvel and Sony it looks like  venom is going to cook up its own  streamlined origin story instead the  venom trailer seems to reveal that  rather than Eddie discovering venom  through spider-man the light foundation  does it also skips the element of  Venom's origin where it masquerades as a  superhero suit the alien that the  foundation discovers is impure symbiote  form there appears to be no intended  trickery on its part the audience and  the film's characters will see it in its  true goopy form from the start and a  goopy venom is a happy venom thanks for  watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our youtube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  you love to  [Music]
 

